{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/192847-ex2-5-abyssal-overdrive-fear-strengthens-the-reaper-peach","id":192847,"title":"[EX2.5] Abyssal Overdrive: Fear Strengthens the Reaper (PEACH)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-09T16:08:36-07:00","id":192847,"title":"[EX2.5] Abyssal Overdrive: Fear Strengthens the Reaper (PEACH)","content":"<i><b>Fear Strengthens the Reaper</b></i><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Native, Overdrive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Artful Maiming Onslaught<br /> <br /> Blood need not be the only thing a deathknight feeds on. For some, fear, hatred, and despair will work just as well. This Charm creates an Overdrive pool with a capacity of ten motes. Initially empty, the Abyssal may accrue offensive motes under the following conditions:<ul><li>The Abyssal comes into or stays in the engagement range of a target who holds a negative Intimacy towards the deathknight (1om drip);</li> <li>The Abyssal reinforces a negative Intimacy or causes one to be formed amongst his enemies (2om);</li> <li>The Abyssal kills a target, the kill being witnessed by someone who holds a negative Intimacy towards the deathknight. (Abyssal gains victim's Permanent Essence in offensive motes).</li> </ul><br /> Regardless of how many enemies threaten the Abyssal, he may only gain one mote every time his DV refreshes in the first case. In the second case, he may only gain two motes, regardless of how many enemies gain or reinforce their negative Intimacies towards him.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Abyssals being short on OD charms, I thought I'd bang one up. I actually made this for the regrettably short-lived Unbound Anima chatgame last year, though I didn't save what I had then before it went down. This is thus a reverse-engineering with a few notes transmitted over IRC with another player, and thus thankfully, logged. I'm playing an Abyssal in a Farewell 2E game playing with 2.5, hence why I'm bringing this back.<br /> <br /> This works best with serial opponents. This Charm won't benefit Darth Vader in Episode IV. However, he gets mote drip during the duel at Cloud City, and gets 2om cutting off Luke's hand (leastways if you work out the cutting as reinforcing a negative Intimacy). He'd continue to have mote drip on the Death Star II until Luke learns to wipe away that Intimacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Journeys know no season.</i>","edited":{"userid":1478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1478-vorshan-saintrowe","user":"Vorshan Saintrowe","date":". 07-10-2014, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1478-vorshan-saintrowe","name":"Vorshan Saintrowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T20:38:44-07:00","id":193070,"title":"","content":"... Isn't the Dusk keyword superfluous for a melee charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T21:24:08-07:00","id":193113,"title":"","content":"That's what I get for copying the top block off Righteous Avenger's Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Journeys know no season.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",